commit d7245765ea9b880729be5478ce098aeefe522dc5
Author: Walter Angolar <angolar.devops@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 20 01:26:34 2026 +0100

    dns: an HTTPRoute can publish its host names through the holder DNS (ADR-0046 phase 1b, WIP)
    
    spec.hosts: [containers] on HTTPRoute (and expose[].hosts) registers each rule host
    in <root>/ingress/route-hosts.json, synced by the proxy composer. The holder DNS
    answers it with the bridge address of the querying client's network.
    
    NOT usable from a container yet: dlxinput drops a container's connection to the
    proxy on that address, on purpose (a container reaching the proxy is relayed to any
    backend, across namespaces). Awaiting a decision; see the ADR.
    
    Also fixes the plan reading routes to a VM as permanent drift.

